Z||000019||California Kid||09-19-2001||08:31 PM||||They see the outside and  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>Notice the Tach and gages  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"><BR>Look at the carbon fiber and leather  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><BR>Walk back to see engine and  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"> followed by  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><BR>Then  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> and  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif"><BR>||||reg||6
Z||000020||Conrad Sanville||09-19-2001||09:20 PM||||The oldest of my 3 Fieros, an '84 I've had since new and now has over 350k on the clock. Noone has bad mouthed the cars to my face.  I can't think of any other car that I could have driven summer and winter and have it as presentable as that car.  I would have thought the fire thing would have died out by now.<P>Quotes from folks almost 18 years now.<P>Must be a handfull in the snow..<P>Is that fibreglass?<P>How do you fit in those things?<P>At least they will never rust....Right.<P>Wow, this thing feels like a go cart. (My '86 GT).<P>Why and when did they stop making them?<P>These cars are sure comfortable.  can't believe the legroom.  <P>How many of those things to you own???!!!||||reg||1
Z||000021||Voytek||09-20-2001||12:41 PM||||Las Friday at the 1/4 mile track - a man walking by with g/f or wife: <BR>'Look.. Fieros   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> '<P>Half an hour later, an over-sized gentleman with his Camaro,  was waiting to race and looking at my car like 'what's th' hell is this  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> '.  Turned out to be the guy I raced and beat.  I would have LOVED to see both of those guys right after the race.<P>Other than that:<BR>'these things aren't safe'<BR>'what kind of car is that'<P>And all kinds of 'WOW, that's a cool car!' from little kids to teenagers.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by Voytek (edited 09-20-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000022||Tigger||09-20-2001||01:05 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Rick 88:<BR><B>"That can't be the stock muffler, it sounds too good."   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>That's funny, last month or so pulling up to a light a guy shouted two lanes over if my exhaust was brand X yadda yadda - (I can't remember).  I could tell he seemed impressed by the sound.  I replied "Nope, all stock"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000023||StuGood||09-20-2001||01:10 PM||||Having owned at least one of these cars for the last 15 years, one hears a variety of comments.  The vast majority have been very positive ones.  A few paraphrased excerpts:<P>(Looking at the long, low front of the car):<BR>"Man, that thing is <B>all</B> hood - I bet the engine's something to see.  What-? It's in back?  Really?  Lemme see!"<P>(After I finished my GT's recent engine work)  "The engine compartment looks real nice - I like the sound, too."   ||||reg||6
Z||000024||Santa Cruzer||09-20-2001||01:18 PM||||the comment's i get from the girl's is "sweet ride man" my girlfriend dosen't like ti much "major corvette fan" so she say's its "ok", my friends like it most of them say man you got a "sick" car!!! or you man io can feel the power this thing has from behind me||||reg||1
Z||000025||MinnGreenGT||09-20-2001||01:38 PM||||Comments?  Varies quite a bit as people have mentioned. <P>I don't get the "...cars that catch on fire..." much anymore.  <P>There a couple of young kids waiting for the bus every morning on my way to work- they wave and cheer as I gun it passing by.<P>My friends are cool about it.  I would never buy the cars they drive -and they would never buy the cars I drive.  But we all get along and know enough about each others cars to enjoy hanging out.<P>On my way down to Fierorama this year, I stopped a McD's for breakfast.  The kid basically asked if it was a Fiero..."yup" ...that's cool, I've never seen one kept in that good of condition.  That's awsome!  (that sure made my day!)<P>Cruising at Porkey's in St.Paul (local car hangout) I get looks, but not many comments.  If I run up the street to the local Ricer hangout (strip mall parking lot behind White Castle- of course). I got A LOT of wierd "what are you doing here" looks and a sarcastic "that's a fast car" from some RicerBoy with a Civic.<P>And at local car shows, especially where I'm the only Fiero, I get the "Fieros aren't too common anymore- that's a nice car" which is quite a compliment from the "Real HotRod" crowd!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/grngtsig3.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/halfpole.gif">  <BR>Medium Metallic Green 87 GT<BR>3.1L High Output<BR>4 Spd OD Tranny<BR>Open (read: Loud) Exhaust<BR>and More!<BR>-Rob Bartlett||||reg||1
